5,1,1,talk,Toshio,,I believe we should prioritize understanding how previous projects have actually performed for the users. I will look into the post-occupancy review ratings and the booking data for specialist and general rooms.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Victoria,,"I agree that usage patterns are key. To complement that, I would like to examine the timetable records on rooms out of service and the post-occupancy review ratings as well.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,George,,I am concerned about the burden on our personnel. I will look into the staffing posts since the hiring freeze and the bench technicians' weekly manual routines.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Mizuki,,I want to ensure our timelines are realistic. I will look into the survey findings in the older blocks and the decade of delivery schedules by project rationale to see where delays typically occur.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems we are all covering the human and temporal elements quite thoroughly. To add a financial perspective, I shall examine the tender records over three budget cycles and the renewal reserve for equipment bought earlier.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Toshio,,"It seems we have a comprehensive spread of data. @Victoria, since we both chose the post-occupancy reviews, I am interested to see if our interpretations of the user satisfaction align.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Toshio, I believe they will. It is important to see if the perceived success of a project matches the actual frequency of its use.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,George,,"I agree. It is one thing to have a facility that looks good on paper, but quite another to ensure it doesn't create more work for the staff maintaining it.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@George, that is a valid point. I believe that understanding the gap between planned schedules and actual delivery will help us avoid placing undue stress on both the staff and the budget.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Benjamin,,"Indeed. It would be a tragedy to select a project based on an optimistic brochure, only to find the market has moved on or the funds have vanished into a void of unforeseen costs.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Toshio,,I think we have a solid plan. I will stick with my choices and wait for the results to see which direction we should take for the improvement plan.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,Victoria,,I concur. I will proceed with the timetable records and post-occupancy reviews to see how construction disruptions and final utility truly impact our campus operations.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,George,,I shall remain with my selection. Understanding the daily grind of our technicians and the current staffing levels is essential for a sustainable decision.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,Mizuki,,I will also stick with my choices. Identifying the root causes of past delays is the only way to ensure our next project doesn't slip into the following year.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Benjamin,,I shall maintain my selections as well. Let us hope the data provides a refreshing dose of reality to our deliberations. I look forward to seeing what the records reveal.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
20,1,4,talk,Toshio,,"Since we have all confirmed our selections and the scope of our investigation is clear, I believe we have exhausted the need for further discussion in this round. I am ready to review the findings.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
21,1,4,talk,Victoria,,"I agree. We have a balanced approach covering usage, staffing, timing, and finance. I am ready to see the results of our research.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
22,1,4,talk,George,,I agree. Let us move forward and see what the evidence tells us about the actual state of our facilities and the people who run them.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
23,1,4,talk,Mizuki,,I agree. We have a comprehensive set of data points to analyze. I look forward to seeing how these findings will shape our final decision for the coming fiscal year.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
24,1,4,talk,Benjamin,,Indeed. It is a rare pleasure to begin a committee meeting with such a methodical approach. I shall await the findings with a mixture of curiosity and a healthy dose of skepticism.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
